        "chapterId": 253,
        "headingId": 1162,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>None</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-31T14:52:01"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1124,
    "bookid": 87,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Localization",
    "headingPosition": 6,
    "headingid": 1163,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 154781,
        "bookId": 87,
        "chapterId": 253,
        "headingId": 1163,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Tumours are superficially located within dermis and/or subcutaneous fat. These lesions occur on the extremities with a large majority located in the hands and feet {29957732; 29309308; 32901982}. Rare extra-acral examples have been reported, mostly affecting lower extremities {29957732; 32901982}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-31T14:52:01"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1125,
    "bookid": 87,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Clinical features",
    "headingPosition": 7,
    "headingid": 1164,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 154782,
        "bookId": 87,
        "chapterId": 253,
        "headingId": 1164,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Patients usually present with a small, painless, superficial tumour in an acral site.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-31T14:52:01"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1126,
    "bookid": 87,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Epidemiology",
    "headingPosition": 8,
    "headingid": 1165,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 154783,
        "bookId": 87,
        "chapterId": 253,
        "headingId": 1165,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The tumours are extremely rare, with &lt;&nbsp;20&nbsp;reported cases to date. There is a wide age range (1&ndash;68&nbsp;years), with a strong female predilection {29957732; 29309308; 32901982}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-31T14:52:01"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1127,
    "bookid": 87,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Etiology",
    "headingPosition": 9,
    "headingid": 1166,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 154784,
        "bookId": 87,
        "chapterId": 253,
        "headingId": 1166,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Unknown</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-31T14:52:01"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1128,
    "bookid": 87,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Pathogenesis",
    "headingPosition": 10,
    "headingid": 1167,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 154785,
        "bookId": 87,
        "chapterId": 253,
        "headingId": 1167,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The tumour is defined by an <em>EWSR1</em>::<em>SMAD3</em> fusion {29957732; 29309308; 32901982}. SMAD3 is an important signal transducer in the TGF-&beta;/SMAD signalling pathway, which is involved in extracellular matrix synthesis by fibroblasts. By RNA sequencing, 1&nbsp;case showed substantial upregulation of <em>FN1</em>, similar to other fibroblastic tumours, as well as ERG overexpression {29309308}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-31T14:52:01"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1135,
    "bookid": 87,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Macroscopic appearance",
    "headingPosition": 11,
    "headingid": 1174,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 154786,
        "bookId": 87,
        "chapterId": 253,
        "headingId": 1174,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The tumours are small, measuring 10&ndash;20&nbsp;mm in greatest dimension, and have a nodular appearance.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-31T14:52:01"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1129,
    "bookid": 87,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Histopathology",
    "headingPosition": 12,
    "headingid": 1168,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 154787,
        "bookId": 87,
        "chapterId": 253,
        "headingId": 1168,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The tumours are typically well demarcated but show infiltration into subcutaneous fat. Superficial cases may directly abut the epidermis. The tumours consist of short intersecting cellular fascicles of monomorphic fibroblastic spindle cells lacking nuclear pleomorphism, hyperchromasia, or prominent nucleoli. Mitotic activity is typically low. The stroma is either collagenous or myxoid. In a subset of cases, a distinctive zonation of central acellular hyalinized areas is discerned, contrasting with the peripheral cellular component. Focally stippled dystrophic calcification may be found. By immunohistochemistry, most cases show diffuse strong ERG nuclear expression in the tumour cells, whereas staining for SMA, CD34, and other relevant markers is negative {29957732; 29309308; 32901982}.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-31T14:52:01"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1130,
    "bookid": 87,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Cytology",
    "headingPosition": 13,
    "headingid": 1169,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 154788,
        "bookId": 87,
        "chapterId": 253,
        "headingId": 1169,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Insufficient data</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-31T14:52:01"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1131,
    "bookid": 87,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Diagnostic molecular pathology",
    "headingPosition": 14,
    "headingid": 1170,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 154789,
        "bookId": 87,
        "chapterId": 253,
        "headingId": 1170,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>The <em>EWSR1</em>::<em>SMAD3</em> fusion or <em>EWSR1</em> gene rearrangement may be confirmed by molecular methods.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-31T14:52:01"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1134,
    "bookid": 87,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Essential and desirable diagnostic criteria",
    "headingPosition": 15,
    "headingid": 1173,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 154790,
        "bookId": 87,
        "chapterId": 253,
        "headingId": 1173,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>Essential:</em> superficial acral nodule; short intersecting cellular fascicles of bland spindle cells with variably hyalinized areas.</p>\r\n<p><em>Desirable:</em> immunoreactivity for ERG; <em>EWSR1</em>::<em>SMAD3</em> fusion or <em>EWSR1</em> gene rearrangement in select cases.</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-31T14:52:01"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1132,
    "bookid": 87,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Staging",
    "headingPosition": 16,
    "headingid": 1171,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 154791,
        "bookId": 87,
        "chapterId": 253,
        "headingId": 1171,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p>Not applicable</p>\r\n",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-31T14:52:01"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  },
  {
    "pkheadingid": 1133,
    "bookid": 87,
    "headingType": 2,
    "headingTitle": "Prognosis and prediction",
    "headingPosition": 17,
    "headingid": 1172,
    "contributions": [
      {
        "pkcontributionId": 154792,
        "bookId": 87,
        "chapterId": 253,
        "headingId": 1172,
        "headingText": "\r\n<p><em>EWSR1</em>::<em>SMAD3</em>&ndash;rearranged fibroblastic tumour is benign. Local recurrences often occur after incomplete excision.</p>",
        "timestamp": "2026-08-31T14:52:01"
      }
    ],
    "booknotes": [],
    "numberofBooknote": 0
  }
]